    "description": "CLAUDE.md or a skill? Per the Claude Code docs, CLAUDE.md loads into every session and costs context on every request. A skill only loads its description at the start and its full content when it's needed. Rule of thumb: what always applies goes in CLAUDE.md; reference material and workflows you start with /<name> go in a skill.",
    "companion_text": "More Claude workflows, step by step: follow Promptwerk. Based on the Claude Code docs (Extend Claude Code, Manage costs effectively), retrieved 2026-11-01. The editor and terminal are an animation, not a screen recording. Limits per the docs: a skill's description is still in every request unless you set disable-model-invocation: true. Claude picks skills by their descriptions; if a description is vague, Claude may load the wrong skill or miss a helpful one.",
